; walk-runaway — the cap, and the diagnostic it raises.
;
; Four rows the walk would play in 24 ticks, stopped after three:
; `:max-rows` is what plan 06's "cap of 2^20 rows trips `walk_runaway`"
; is for, since a module whose timing state never repeats would otherwise
; walk for ever. The map keeps the rows it played, there is no loop
; point, and the diagnostic is an error.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk :max-rows 3)
